  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing conflict affected populations safety and protection in 3 southern oblasts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project involves implementation of 3 main activities: - Non Technical Survey (NTS)/Explosive Ordnance Risk Eduation (EORE) in Kherson region (1000 beneficiaries)-EORE/Conflict Preparednes &amp; Protection (&#x421;PP) sessions in Odesa (8400 beneficiaries)-EORE/First Aid (FA) sessions in Mykolaiv region (2500 beneficiaries)  All the in-field activities shall be conducted by mobile EORE/CPP, EORE/NTS and EORE/FA teams. The project starts with a 2 weeks preparation stage,  consisting of ToT (Trainings for Trainers) to refresh the knowledge of EORE/CPP, NTS and FA teams and procurement of all necessary equipment and handouts materials according to the budget.The next part are the NTS, EORE/CPP and FA activities in regions, that will last for 6,5 months . This activity includes entry visit of EORE/CPP, EORE/NTS and EORE/FA teams to regions. They will have a conversation with local authorities about future project activities in the area and managing local coordination efforts. Direct communication with local authorities will allow to obtain the most actual information about the security environment and demographic indicators.The final stage of the project will include 1 month data summarizing and reporting.</narrative>
  </description>
